Read frames back after the frame instead of in the middle of flip

Without the frontend's Vulkan device, each frame is copied back for the
frontend. The immediate copy waits for the GPU inside flip. When a game's
display format differs from its back buffer, get_present_source flips from
a temporary image it has already handed to the texture cache to dispose
of, and that wait completes the frame, so the image is freed while flip
still blits from it. In Kodi, Mortal Kombat vs. DC Universe deadlocked at
its first logo on the heap this corrupted. The deferred copy, already
there, runs with the rest of the frame and is handed over once the frame
has finished.

--- a/rpcs3/libretro/libretro_core.cpp
+++ b/rpcs3/libretro/libretro_core.cpp
@@ -984,9 +984,10 @@ static void libretro_apply_core_options()
 
     g_libretro_frontend_vblank = get_option_value("rpcs3_frame_pacing", "emulator") == "frontend";
 
-    // Immediate: the readback path is only the fallback without the
-    // frontend's Vulkan device now, and no longer offered as an option.
-    g_libretro_deferred_readback = false;
+    // Deferred: the immediate copy waits for the GPU in the middle of flip,
+    // and the temporary image a display format conversion flips from is
+    // freed by that wait while flip still uses it
+    g_libretro_deferred_readback = true;
 
     // Driver Wake-Up Delay
     std::string driver_delay = get_option_value("rpcs3_driver_wakeup_delay", "0");
